; A nested `region` reusing an enclosing region's name.
;
; Regions are ordered by NESTING - MM-RGN-2 of
; docs/memory-model-v2-design.md: an inner region's extent is inside
; its enclosing one's, and that is the whole of what "outlives" means
; for them. A name that named two open extents at once could not be
; placed in that order, so the checker keeps the stack of open regions
; (`checkRegion`, `self_host/typecheck.ax`) and refuses the reuse while
; the outer one is open. Nothing can refer to a region by name yet;
; when a `@r` in type position can (S3), it resolves against this
; stack, which is why the rule exists before the reference does.
;
; The two SIBLING regions at the end share a name and must be silent:
; each opens and closes in turn, and the stack never holds both.
; The anchor is the inner NAME token, not the keyword - the name is
; what has to change.
(import IO)

(:: main Int)

(fn (main)
  {
    (region r
      (region r 0))
    (region s 1)
    (region s 2)
  })
